#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115100 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af60bcc-de12-52a1-b0b0-9485ed497126" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Difference of Squares in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "1eaa26ba-0958-58db-9f30-35a33f98f2d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5121" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac {x^2 - 9} {(x + 3)(x+2)}$." :question/worked-solution "The numerator is a difference of squares. If we factor it and then cancel out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {x^2 - 9} {(x + 3)(x+2)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {(x + 3)(x - 3)} {(x + 3)(x+2)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {\\cancel{(x + 3)}(x - 3)} {\\cancel{(x + 3)}(x+2)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {x - 3} {x+2} &. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115101 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22de4ff5-a317-5d89-a9da-80d40648f2e1" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "fb69899e-6aee-5128-973e-e19792a1cbdb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5122" :question/problem "What is $\\dfrac {x^2 + x - 6} {x-2}$ reduced to lowest terms?" :question/worked-solution "The numerator can be factored as\n\n$$\nx^2+x-6= (x+3)(x-2)\n$$\n\nCancelling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2} + x - 6}{x - 2} &=  \\\\\n((x + 3)(x - 2))/(x - 2) &=  \\\\\n((x + 3)(x - 2))/((x - 2)) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{x + 3}{1} &=  \\\\\n&= x + 3 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115102 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7321f2-f17f-5d22-a0d1-02720b3a6dc5" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "fd181873-1190-5ffa-b2aa-c7eb68c1255c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5123" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2a^2+4ab+2b^2}$." :question/worked-solution "Here, we take out a factor of $2$ from the denominator, and then use the polynomial factorization\n\n$$\na^2+2ab+b^2 = (a+b)^2\n$$\n\nCancelling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2a^2+4ab+2b^2} &=\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2\\left(a^2+2ab+b^2\\right)} \\\\ &=\\dfrac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot(a+b)} {2(a+b)(a+b)} \\\\ &=\\dfrac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot\\cancel{(a+b)}} {\\cancel{2}\\cancel{(a+b)}(a+b)} \\\\ &=\\dfrac {2} {a+b}. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115104 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "1e777ba3-6a10-5c47-b069-ee33a6892a98" :question/math-academy-id "e-5313" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x^2-5x+6}$." :question/worked-solution "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2} - 4}{x^{2} - 5x + 6} &= ((x - 2)(x + 2))/((x - 3)(x - 2)) \\\\\n&= ((x - 2)(x + 2))/((x - 3)(x - 2)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{x + 2}{x - 3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e8f883d-2ec6-5aef-a22a-ceb67aa75048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{2} - 3}{y^{2} - 2y + 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112040} {:answer/id #uuid "1805dbc5-c2e9-5837-9988-9d368505f6de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{2} - 9}{y^{2} - 6y + 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112041} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9b336c-cd1f-5f68-918e-fb100610e033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y + 3}{y - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112042} {:answer/id #uuid "551c34b1-dcf8-53db-988c-a56cb45643ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112043} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce516fc-eed1-5dfd-9c94-b704a4e66dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y - 3}{y + 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112044}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8abb5688-150a-50b2-9719-9f49715e34e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112039}] :question/id #uuid "6dd5bac7-d40e-5521-a7ba-7380ff2d57e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-150" :question/problem "What is $\\frac{y^{2} - 9}{y^{2} - 6y + 9}$ reduced to lowest terms?"}]}
